The mock tree `scratchpad/sf-city-anim/` is 12 GB and is not in this repository;
`_bldgsrc.py` replays its output rather than holding its source. So a change to
a mock builder has nowhere in git to live, and this directory is where it lives:
one unified diff per change, applied from the mock root.

    cd scratchpad/sf-city-anim && patch -p0 < <this file>
    python3 bldg/build_bldg.py          # rewrites gen/bldg-data.js

2026-08-24 — THE BLOCK KEY. `build_bldg.py` keyed its block fallback on
`pn[:4]`, which is the assessor block only when the block is four characters.
401 of San Francisco's 5,413 published blocks are five — four digits and a
letter — so the key pooled 4591A, 4591B, 4591C and 4591D into one bucket and
dated an 11,719 m2, 52 m Navy industrial hall on 4591A from the 25th-percentile
year of 4591C's 523 Hunters Point Shipyard Phase 1 condominium rows: 2015.
219 buildings arrived in that one frame.

The block is published — acdm-wktn ships `block_num` and `lot_num` as separate
columns — so `pnjoin.py`, the file that already states the PARCEL join key once
so two files cannot drift, now states the BLOCK key too.

Measured over the rebuilt gen/bldg-data.js: 534 of 166,166 buildings change
year, 303 by twenty years or more; year 2015 loses 220; the shipyard's 219
split into 158 at 1989 (block 4591A's own p25) and 68 at 2016 (4591C's, and
those 68 are the condominiums). See DATA-TRUTH.md section 7.

